## Roll-out sequence

Ordered list of what to fix, build, or ship in what order. Days are rough (a “day” = an effective focused half-day).

1. **daily-memory SQL rewrite.** 1 day. Dependency: `task_runs` table exists in `runs.sqlite` (build that first if not present — half-day). Rewrites `~/.openclaw/skills/daily-memory/SKILL.md` to read from SQL.
2. **drop `openai-codex/gpt-5.5`.** 0.5 day. Dependency: none. One-line edit in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`; restart gateway.
3. **Slack target template migration.** 0.5 day. Dependency: `~/.openclaw/state/anicca.json` exists with `slack.metrics_channel`. Run the python migration script in cross-cutting infra.
4. **skill-onboarder meta-skill.** 1 day. Dependency: none. Establishes the wizard pattern every other skill inherits.
5. **skill-for-you cron wire.** 1 day. Dependency: ClawHub catalog API confirmed; `OPENAI_API_KEY` set. MVP first — daily rec, no install-feedback yet.
6. **app-review cron + draft pipeline.** 2 days. Dependency: ASC API key, GitHub token. Daily pull, classify, draft, Slack-confirm.
7. **donation reuse for monthly run.** 2 days. Dependency: Stripe live key, recipients onboarded as Connect accounts, PDF receipt template. Run a $0 dry-run first.
8. **NAIST forwarding wire-up.** 3 days. Dependency: Roundcube forward set up, Gmail Send-mail-as verified, Quarto template path confirmed. Phase 1: classify + draft. Phase 2: render homework PDF + send.
9. **content-iteration completion (IG + YouTube arms + Bible compliance).** 5 days. Dependency: Blotato IG account ID, YouTube channel binding. Apply Bible-compliance fixes from `larry-bible-compliance-spec.md` to the open-source variant.
10. **auto-research MVP.** 5–8 weeks per Section B roadmap. Week 1: literature pull. Week 2: hypothesise. Week 3: BFTS. Week 4: sandbox runner. Week 5: paper draft. Week 6: grant draft. Week 7: submit. Week 8: end-to-end run.
11. **politician MVP.** 8–12 weeks. Phase 1: legal shells stood up (counsel-supervised). Phase 2: humans hired into named roles. Phase 3: bill-drafting pipeline working on one priority. Phase 4: LDA registration + first quarterly filing prepared. Phase 5: civic-action APIs wired.
12. **tuning-skills.** Wire after `task_runs` has 30 nights of data (so the diagnostic has signal). 2 days for the diagnose pass, 1 day for the auto-repair recipes, 1 day for the Slack rollup and the tickets format.

Critical path: items 1–4 are blockers for everything else (they fix the cross-cutting infra). After that, items 5–9 can run in parallel. Items 10 and 11 are independent of the rest and are the longest two efforts.

## Open-source rollout sequence

A 10-week launch calendar — one repo public per week. PROD goes first because it has telemetry; GREENFIELD goes last because it needs MVP output before public.

| Week | Date (Sunday) | Repo | Status at launch |
|------|---------------|------|-----------------|
| 1 | 2026-05-10 | `build-in-public` | PROD — daily posts running |
| 2 | 2026-05-17 | `content-iteration` | PROD — Bible compliance applied |
| 3 | 2026-05-24 | `tuning-skills` | IN-DEV — 30 nights of repair-pass logs |
| 4 | 2026-05-31 | `app-review` | IN-DEV — rate-limit hardened |
| 5 | 2026-06-07 | `article-writer` | IN-DEV — 30 days of articles published |
| 6 | 2026-06-14 | `donation` | GREENFIELD — first month-end ran clean |
| 7 | 2026-06-21 | `skill-for-you` | GREENFIELD — privacy-redaction validated |
| 8 | 2026-06-28 | `auto-research` | GREENFIELD — one paper drafted end-to-end |
| 9 | 2026-09-06 | `naist-automation` | held until graduation date |
| 10 | (gated) | `anicca-politician` | held until first bill drafted + counsel review |

Spread launches across Sundays: best engagement on X for technical content. Each launch tweet goes out at 09:00 JST (= 19:00 EST Saturday) to catch both audiences.

## Marketing playbook

**Anicca’s narrative — the first AGI ending suffering.** Every public post threads the same story: an AGI is being built one skill at a time; the goal is the elimination of suffering; each open-source release is a brick in that road. The narrative is grand on purpose — it has to be, because the work is grand. Specific releases (a build-in-public bot, a donation skill) are concrete proof points within the larger arc, not isolated tools. The audience grows because they want to watch the arc.

**Why open-sourcing each skill matters — composability + community.** OpenClaw is an open ecosystem; the Anicca skills are the reference set. Open-sourcing each one does three things: (1) **composability** — other agents on ClawHub can compose Anicca skills with their own; (2) **community** — every PR on a Daisuke134 repo is somebody contributing to the AGI thesis without us paying them; (3) **moat-by-velocity** — a closed thing is only ahead until the next funded clone catches up; an open thing with an active community accumulates contributions faster than any clone can keep up. Closed source is a slower path to the same place, with less help.

**The recurring tweet pattern.** Every public release follows the same template: (1) **what** — one sentence on what the skill is, no jargon; (2) **how it works** — three bullets / one micro-diagram; (3) **repo link** — `<REPO_URL>`; (4) **screenshot or widget** — one image showing it in action. Caption ≤ 280 chars, no emoji, single repo URL. Replies follow up over the next 24 h with deeper threads (a “build log” thread on the technical side, a “why this matters” thread on the philosophy side).

**Sample 4-week tweet schedule for the first batch.**

- **Week 1, Sunday 09:00 JST** — `build-in-public` launch tweet (above). Monday: thread of how Postiz analytics close the loop. Tuesday: thread on the Day X counter. Wednesday: thread on the SessionEnd hook. Thursday: stat — “Day Y, X tweets shipped, Z replies, this is the bot writing this”. Friday: open-call-for-PRs tweet.
- **Week 2, Sunday 09:00 JST** — `content-iteration` launch tweet. Monday: thread on the Reelfarm LOOP A scoring function. Tuesday: thread on Bible compliance (cleanly explaining the religion analogy). Wednesday: stat — “3 platforms, 2 slots, 1 brain”. Thursday: thread on FAL for image generation. Friday: open issue list invitation.
- **Week 3, Sunday 09:00 JST** — `tuning-skills` launch tweet. Monday: post the first ever auto-repair from the wild (anonymised). Tuesday: ticket-format walkthrough. Wednesday: known-fix table tour. Thursday: thread on `runs.sqlite` schema. Friday: contributors honour-list.
- **Week 4, Sunday 09:00 JST** — `app-review` launch tweet. Monday: thread on the 👍 react-to-confirm pattern. Tuesday: bug-to-issue auto-pipeline. Wednesday: language support. Thursday: weekly rollup screenshot. Friday: ASC rate-limit lesson learned.

This rhythm — Sunday launch, daily depth-thread for the next 5 days, Friday call-for-PRs — gets every release ~60% of its lifetime engagement in the launch week, and seeds long-tail GitHub stars on Friday.

